{
  "allocation_derivation": [
    "The callback is limited to the two exact original228-byte factory97/FE-add requests with Half[2] raw words1,2 and the original dense F32[2] right operand.",
    "Require equal actual before/after slots and pool capacity. A capacity-growing owner is explicitly outside this finite predicate and cannot pass.",
    "For each of the three source-proved descriptor indices, allocate an internal page only when its page index is absent, then allocate data Storage of4,8,8 bytes respectively.",
    "Select T/S/V slots by so_slot_new: first nonlive slot with generation below0xffffffff, then generation+1. No hardcoded capability, slot, generation or owner address is used.",
    "Select Storage offsets by so_extent_allocate: first sufficient actual before free extent, align requested size to16, remove an exact extent or advance its start.",
    "The sole temporary promotion frees exactly its16-byte aligned allocation. so_extent_release restores sorted, adjacent-coalesced free extents; compare the complete observed final free list.",
    "Construct all three84-word descriptors from source constants and the derived handles/offsets/index/incarnation. All other words are required zero. Compare every T/S/V row, including unchanged old rows and generation-preserving retired rows.",
    "alloc creates Storage then Hold. Derive each Hold slot from the evolving expected Hold table by first nonlive, non-exhausted generation; increment generation and write [generation,1,Storage,1,0,0,0,0]. A page retains its Hold, while typed_descriptor immediately drops each data Hold to [generation,0,0,0,0,0,0,0]. A reused Hold slot therefore advances once per allocation.",
    "Compare every word of all eight complete owner tables. Weak, Saved, Generator, and Optimizer kinds4,5,7,8 are exactly unchanged including dead rows; kind6 includes exact retained page Holds and exact generation-preserving data-Hold retirement."
  ],
  "cleanup_derivation": [
    "finish_command changes temporary node200=2 to0. Published factory and result are1 and survive. graph_collect_since enqueues the sole unreachable node whose node304=1,node200=0,node208=0.",
    "retained_gc_enqueue_original changes node432 to1 and node424 to0 (queue linkage). graph_collect_since clears both node424 and432 before graph_node_release, so words53 and54 are zero after cleanup.",
    "graph_node_release sees node600=0. dtype_mask_release/mixed_original_mask_release return without writes because node584=592=0. history_accumulator_target returns0 while node240=1, and history_accumulator_release returns because node624=0. graph_node_release explicitly zeroes node608/624/632.",
    "dtype_original_graph_node_release checks node312/88/400 all0. node40=0 skips parent-edge release. saved_release(0) at node280/288/296 and hold_release(0) at node248/256/264/272 are immediate no-ops.",
    "tensor_row_release -> view_previous_tensor_row_release -> mixed_original_tensor_row_release -> dtype_original_tensor_row_release -> retained_row_release_original. node600=0 and retained_temporary_root sees Trow flags.word7&2==0, so release is not deferred.",
    "gradient_binding sees node384/392/360 all0 and returns0, so gradient_unbind writes nothing. retained_row_release_original releases V, then S, then T, and writes exactly node240=0.",
    "V has sole ref1: so_version_release calls so_slot_drop(kind3). S has refs1 and weak_refs1: so_storage_release frees the original16-byte extent and drops kind2. T drops kind1. so_slot_drop zeros row bytes8..63 and preserves row generation; it does not clear descriptor identity fields.",
    "to_view_base_release sees node664=640=648=656=0 and writes nothing. Any repeated mask check returns without writes. dtype_original_graph_node_release finally writes node304=0.",
    "No cleanup path writes the retained data pointer, base index, rank/count/shape/stride, T/S/V handles, or incarnation. Therefore all84 words are determined by the constructor and the enumerated zeroing; not just dead flags."
  ],
  "constructor_derivation": [
    "scalar_previous_typed_descriptor b37 zeros the entire 672-byte descriptor before assigning rank, dtype, numel, requires_grad, owned-storage base index, root state2, live state1, and incremented incarnation.",
    "For dtype0, rank1, shape[2], requires_grad0 and allocate_storage1: words0=1,1=2,4=0,8=index,25=2,38=1,40=new incarnation,72=0. b39 writes only shape word12=2 and stride word16=1.",
    "b40 creates T; words24=T,30=1. b41 allocates exactly8 logical data bytes; alloc aligns capacity to16, creates S and Hold, and stores S refs1/weak_refs1. b44 creates V with refs1, stores data in word2 and S/V in words27/28, then drops Hold. b45 skips all gradient allocation because requires_grad0.",
    "alloc stores extent_return-1 in Storage row.word2 and returns (1<<63)+extent_return-1; this is descriptor.word2. No cleanup path clears the descriptor data pointer.",
    "Dense shape[2] dist_dense_layout leaves stride1. Copy arithmetic writes data bytes only; no history, views, saved tensors, graph edges or retained references are created. right F32 promotion returns the old operand unchanged."
  ],
  "constructor_sequence": [
    "Half factory node at before_next_descriptor; incarnation before_incarnation+1",
    "left promotion to F32 node at before_next_descriptor+1; incarnation before_incarnation+2",
    "F32 result node at before_next_descriptor+2; incarnation before_incarnation+3"
  ],
